165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (This report presents the design and implementation of Egg Catcher Master, a 2D desktop arcade game developed in Python using the standard tkinter graphical user interface \(GUI\) framework. The project demonstrates the practical application of event-driven programming, object movement, dynamic collision detection, and game loop mechanics without relying on heavy third-party game engines.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (The game core loop involves catching randomly generated, multi-colored eggs falling from the top of the screen using a user-controlled basket mapped to the keyboard's left and right arrow keys. To enhance engagement and replayability, an exponential difficulty scaling algorithm was implemented; as the player's score increases, the interval delay between animation frames decreases, causing the eggs to accelerate dynamically.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
