175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (In the field of software engineering, game development serves as an excellent vehicle for mastering core programming paradigms, such as real-time state management, asynchronous event loops, and graphical user interface \(GUI\) interactions. While modern, feature-rich frameworks like Pygame or Unity are typically preferred for complex 2D and 3D productions, building a game from scratch using native, lightweight libraries offers deeper insights into the fundamental mechanics of computer graphics and event-driven architectures.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (This report details the development of Egg Catcher Master, a 2D desktop arcade game implemented entirely in Python using tkinter, the standard built-in GUI toolkit. The primary objective of this project was to construct a responsive, engaging game loop and physics system utilizing only foundational system libraries, avoiding the overhead of heavy third-party dependencies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
