181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Developing a real-time interactive game within a standard, non-gaming GUI framework like Python's tkinter presents several fundamental software engineering challenges. Traditional desktop GUI applications are designed to be passive, waiting silently for a user to click a button or type text before executing a piece of code.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (By contrast, an arcade game requires an active environment where the system must constantly update graphics, track physics, and manage game states independently of user interaction.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (The core problems this project seeks to address are:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 630 0 R
/E (The Single-Thread Concurrency Problem: How to simulate continuously falling objects \(the eggs\) while simultaneously listening for real-time user keyboard inputs \(moving the basket\) without freezing the application.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 631 0 R
/E (Vector Spatial Collision: Accurately mapping and calculating overlapping coordinates between two irregular shapes \(a flat tkinter canvas oval and an open arc basket\) to determine a valid "catch.")
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 632 0 R
/E (Egg Spawning: create_egg\(\) schedules itself to run every 1500 milliseconds, ensuring a steady stream of new objects.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 633 0 R
/E (Egg Animation: move_eggs\(\) continuously updates the vertical position of all active eggs. By using .after\(egg_speed, move_eggs\), the game creates a seamless animation loop that runs in the background, leaving the main thread completely free to instantly register keyboard inputs.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
